# shir_nodes/string_contains.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# Substring test (lowered from `grep -q`, `case *P*)`).
#
# Backends: Perl index()!=-1, JS .includes(), C strstr(), Rust .contains()
# Fallback: sh2.contains(text, pattern)
#
# The test is the CUT primitives' answer as a boolean: ShIR_TextOps_Cut proves
# `string_contains_sound` — the node is `find_first text pattern != None`, which
# is equivalently "the pattern occurs as a slice of the text", with the empty
# pattern occurring everywhere and the empty TEXT containing only the empty
# pattern. Every backend arm above computes one of those three readings.

node StringContains
tag "StringContains"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field pattern: expr
spec: TextOps#string_contains_sound
